motion-lab-grok-bot
===================

This plugin adapts the motion-design method published by Florence (@flxrnc)
in the X article "Opus 5.5 Motion Lab: Make Claude Animate Like a Studio"
(posted 2026-09-30).

Original work:  "Motion Lab" article by Florence (@flxrnc)
Source:         https://x.com/flxrnc/status/2105311836190978392
                (article: https://x.com/i/article/2105052379590578176)
Author site:    https://www.imflorence.xyz/

Packaged by:    Pedro Gonzalez / Blueforce Innovations

Adapted from the article (prompts and techniques are hers):
- The directed-prompt template, the render contract, the ban list, the motion
  numbers (easing table, damping-ratio rule, durations, stagger, beat grid,
  holds), the render/look/fix lab loop, the follow-up library, the fixes
  table, the sound rules and the X export settings and limits
  (skills/motion-lab/references/, templates/).
- kit/motion.js builds on the article's tokens file and closed-form spring.
- scripts/render.mjs, contact-sheet.sh and export.sh build on the article's
  renderer and ffmpeg commands.
- examples/earbuds, examples/liquid-chrome and examples/mascot reproduce the
  article's prompts and every follow-up, rebranded: the original accent color
  became 2F9C95, the liquid-chrome title became "STUDIO" (drop and note counts
  adjusted), and the mascot became an original voxel robot. Timings,
  materials, lights, springs and measurements are unchanged.

Changed for Grok Bot and Cursor:
- Removed model names, effort/fast-mode settings, pricing, the chat-app
  preview path and coding-agent install steps from the original.
- Rewrote the loop for an agent working on a box: Shell runs the scripts,
  images are read inline, results are attached as MP4/GIF files.
- render.mjs uses playwright-core with system Chrome, waits for
  window.__ready, takes size/fps/duration from arguments, supports stills,
  frame ranges and subframe motion blur, and uses software WebGL when there
  is no GPU.

Original to this plugin: audio-render.mjs, audio-hits.mjs, audio-check.sh,
frame-diff.sh, loop-check.sh, examples/title-loop, the starter templates,
the logo and the screenshot.

Not included: the article's videos and images.

The article was published without a license. This is an independent
adaptation with credit and is not an official release by the original
author. Florence's prompts and text remain hers; on request from the author
the adapted material will be changed or removed.
